---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/sections/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/global/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/global/Button.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Scholarships" description="Learn about Wayfinders scholarships, progressive tuition, transportation support, and the community scholarship fund.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Financial accessibility" title="Scholarships" intro="Wayfinders believes that tuition should not prevent anyone from joining and participating in our community."><div class="actions"><Button href="https://forms.gle/8o8xWUZpeAeRBiYA8">Contribute to the scholarship fund</Button><Button href="https://forms.gle/9iMYsTESrsyxFUAS8" variant="secondary">Apply for a scholarship</Button></div></PageHero>
  <Section width="prose"><div class="policy"><h2 class="type-section">Wayfinders Scholarship Policy</h2><p>Funding does not yet allow for need-blind admission. Families who can are asked to pay full tuition to offset tuition for families unable to pay the full amount. Wayfinders progressive tuition and scholarship opportunities are a step toward creating equity. This effort relies on our community to uplift each other.</p><p>Scholarships draw directly from the <strong>Wayfinders Scholarship Fund</strong>, which is an ongoing fundraising priority. When these funds are depleted, typically no additional scholarships are available for that program year.</p><p>Scholarship applications are processed, and scholarship decisions are made, by a subcommittee of the Wayfinders Board of Directors. The members of this committee are responsible for executing the scholarship process according to the mission and values of the organization, with integrity and impartiality.</p><p>There are limited opportunities for families to provide in-kind donations of goods or services to help offset tuition, depending on organizational needs at a given time.</p><p>Families seeking scholarships can apply directly through the registration form and may select from a range of options. A Scholarship Committee member may follow up with the family directly with additional questions and may request documentation of free and reduced lunch designation.</p></div></Section>
  <Section tone="alternate"><div class="support-grid"><article><h2 class="type-card">Transportation assistance</h2><p>Our parent-coordinated program connects families in need of rides with other participants.</p></article><article><h2 class="type-card">Snacks</h2><p>Snacks are available at programs.</p></article><article><h2 class="type-card">Sibling discounts</h2><p>Reach out to discuss sibling discounts.</p><a href="mailto:wayfindersonthehudson@gmail.com">Contact Wayfinders</a></article></div></Section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.75rem;margin-top:2rem}.policy p{color:var(--color-ink-muted);font-size:1.08rem}.support-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}.support-grid article{padding:var(--card-padding);border:1px solid var(--color-line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);background:var(--color-surface)}.support-grid h2{margin:0}.support-grid p{color:var(--color-ink-muted)}@media(max-width:47.999rem){.actions :global(.button){width:100%}.support-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
